  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8909a7b854c460945b7273a620ed017e, type: 3}
  m_Name: PoI_03_Mr Watson
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: Mr Watson
  characterAvatar: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 99f6b8bcd4e45cd4da781657f40b06ce, type: 3}
  arrivalPrompt: "As a choirister in the 1970s, a lifetime of memories about the
    Cathedral stays with Mr Watson. Even after the earthquakes, he has continued
    to follow the Cathedral's story. He knows its stories intimately \u2014 and believes
    that even its stones have stories to tell."
  arrivalButtonText: Meet Mr Watson
  dialogueLines:
  - Hello, young friend. What a pleasure to see you here.
  - "Sorry, I haven\u2019t introduced myself yet. I\u2019m William Watson\u2014most
    people call me Mr. Watson. I used to sing in the Cathedral Choir when I was a
    young boy, and later when I became a teacher, I brought my students here every
    year."
  - There were always a few who wandered off or lost their way! I used to remind
    them to look for the Cathedral's spire to find their way back.
  - I have many memories of this Cathedral. Some are carved in stone, some can be
    seen in its windows, and some can still be heard in music.
  - "While you\u2019re here, look out for interactive hotspots along the wall\u2014you
    can tap them to see more details. Take your time, and remember you can always
    pause, put down the tablet, and take in the real space around."
  voiceClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ccc6627e40675a2499ca56bc76b69f10, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 85ff07efcdbc74144920707f7f09bbc1, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a68c85653f885704c9b56e44c6293321, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 36959112421f5a94d86f7665cc9ba0f5, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5afaee1a5bfd5c3429ec113c9a0cd0b6, type: 3}
  alignmentPrompt: 
  alignmentButtonText: 
  interactionInstruction: Walk along the panel, and bring your tablet closer to it
    and discover 3 hotspots related to Mr Watson's memory.
  interactionButtonText: Start Exploring
  reflectionPrompt: '"What do you think makes a place worth remembering?"'
  reflectionButtonText: Continue
